/proc/ioports - serial ports

sudo grep -i "serial" /proc/ioports > ex1.txt

dma1 - direct memory access controllerr 1
(allows to transfer data directly to and from
system RAM without tying up the CPU for every byte)

pic1 - programmable interrupt controller 1
(manages hardware interrupt requests from peripheral devices,
like keyboard or timer. and prioritize which signals get sent
to the CPU)

timer1 - programmable interval timer
(generates periodic clock ticks (interrupts) and set intervals.
the system uses these ticks to keep track of time, schedule processes
and manage multitasking)